<article class="env-definition" id="008J">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/008J">Definition <span data-tag="008J">6.21.7</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to Y$ be a continuous map. Let $\mathcal{F}$ be a sheaf of sets on $X$ and let $\mathcal{G}$ be a sheaf of sets on $Y$. An <em>$f$-map $\xi : \mathcal{G} \to \mathcal{F}$</em> is a collection of maps $\xi _ V : \mathcal{G}(V) \to \mathcal{F}(f^{-1}(V))$ indexed by open subsets $V \subset Y$ such that </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ \mathcal{G}(V) \ar[r]_{\xi _ V} \ar[d]_{\text{restriction of }\mathcal{G}} &  \mathcal{F}(f^{-1}V) \ar[d]^{\text{restriction of }\mathcal{F}} \\  \mathcal{G}(V') \ar[r]^{\xi _{V'}} &  \mathcal{F}(f^{-1}V') }  \]
</div>
  <p> commutes for all $V' \subset V \subset Y$ open. </p>
</article>